# Drafted by Gemini (R16 camp), edited.

~ arrival
cutscene sk_glitterdeep
Narrator: You come over the rise to the old camp, where a black timber headframe straddles a square pit breathing up green gas.
cutscene sk_glitterdeep_2
Narrator: The painted board over the yard hangs crooked in the damp wind, welcoming nobody at all.
cutscene end
set sk_arrived
if not quest.skitter_plague >= skitterdeep
quest skitter_plague skitterdeep
endif
-> END

~ sign
Narrator: The board over the warehouse reads Skitterdeep. Someone painted over the first two letters, and that fresh daub of tar is nowhere near seventy years old.
set sk_sign_read
-> END

~ foreman_board
Narrator: The rotted board still holds a peeling shift rota and a hurried note in a woman's hand: burn incense or scented lamps in the lower drifts to keep the thin things off.
-> END

~ handprints
Narrator: The grey dust on the floorboards is dimpled with small, five-fingered tracks.
* [Survival DC 14] Read the handprints in the dust -> hp_ok | hp_fail
* Move on -> END

~ hp_ok
Narrator: A hundred little palms patter back and forth from the middle room, left by something long that walks upon its hands.
-> END

~ hp_fail
Narrator: It is only old mine dust, scuffed and settled thick as flour.
-> END

~ surcoats
Narrator: Folded in the damp corner lie wine-red surcoats stitched with a white tower, stacked beside stiff horse blankets that still smell faintly of oats and old blood.
set surcoats_seen
-> END

~ winch
Narrator: A great iron drum sits cold in its frame, heavy chain threaded through the floor port beside a rusted lever.
-> winch_menu

~ winch_menu
* [Investigation DC 14] Study the winch -> study_ok | study_fail
* [if item:oil] Oil the gears first -> oiled
* Throw the lever as it is -> loud
* [Sleight of Hand DC 15] Jam the drum with thieves' tools -> jam_ok | jam_fail
* Leave it -> END

~ study_ok
Narrator: The teeth are dry and crusted with red rust; work that lever raw and the whole mountain will hear it shriek, though a flask of oil would hush the iron.
set winch_studied
-> winch_menu

~ study_fail
Narrator: It is a lump of old iron and grease, stubborn as a mule and twice as heavy.
-> winch_menu

~ oiled
Narrator: You soak the dry teeth in lamp oil and pull the lever; the chain pays out with nothing louder than a greasy sigh.
take oil
set sk_lift_ready
-> END

~ loud
Narrator: The dry drum shrieks down the shaft like a pig at a wedding, and far below in the wet dark, something stops to listen.
set sk_lift_ready
set skitterdeep_alert = now
-> END

~ jam_ok
Narrator: You wedge an iron spike deep into the teeth until the drum is locked fast; no one is riding this cage tonight.
-> END

~ jam_fail
Narrator: Your pick slips from the greasy cog and the drum lets out an almighty iron howl.
-> loud

~ lift
Narrator: Thirty feet down the black shaft, rough planks sit bolted across three iron beams, swinging gently over the drop.
* [if flag.sk_hoard_taken and flag.sk_lift_ready] Haul the ore boxes up on the lift -> overload
* [if flag.sk_hoard_taken] Haul the ore up by the chain instead -> chain_haul
* Test the planks -> test
* Step back -> END

~ test
Narrator: The damp timber groans under a boot heel, sound enough for a few strong souls, and not an ounce more.
-> END

~ chain_haul
Narrator: You haul the heavy boxes up link by greasy link, which takes three long trips and a great deal of quiet swearing.
-> END

~ overload
Narrator: The winch drum groans under the dead weight of the ore boxes and the cage shudders on its chain.
cutscene sk_lift_falls
cutscene sk_lift_falls_2
Narrator: With a crack like a musket shot the rusted links part, and the whole platform drops into the dark with you aboard.
cutscene end
set skitterdeep_lift_fell
set skitterdeep_alert = now
damage 4d6 bludgeoning party
move sk_deep:from_shaft

~ eyeball
Narrator: Something small and wet shifts among the timber braces overhead.
-> eye_menu

~ eye_menu
* [Perception DC 15] Look closer at the ceiling -> eye_found | eye_missed
* [Arcana DC 15] Unpick the working on it -> eye_dealt | eye_resists
* Cut it down -> eye_cut
* Leave it -> END

~ eye_found
Narrator: A single pale eyeball dangles from the beam by its own slick nerve, turning slowly to keep you in its sight.
set sk_eyeball_found
-> eye_menu

~ eye_missed
Narrator: There is nothing overhead but weeping stone and old cobwebs.
-> eye_menu

~ eye_dealt
Narrator: You pluck the foul thread of magic loose, and the dangling eye clouds over like a boiled fish's.
set sk_eyeball_dealt
-> END

~ eye_resists
Narrator: The greasy little knot of witchcraft slips through your fingers and pulls tight again.
-> eye_menu

~ eye_cut
Narrator: A quick flat blade parts the nerve, and the thing drops into the dirt with a wet pop.
set sk_eyeball_dealt
-> END

~ hoard
if flag.oswald_slain
Narrator: With the glamour broken, the heap is nothing now but cold offal and knucklebones going sour in the dark.
-> END
endif
Narrator: In the last chamber lies a regular dragon's bed of ruby goblets, bright coin, and folded silks gleaming in the dark.
-> hoard_menu

~ hoard_menu
* [Investigation DC 15] Look closely at the heap -> hoard_seen | hoard_blind
* [if flag.sk_hoard_seen and not flag.sk_hoard_taken] Take the real box of nuggets -> real
* Scoop a handful of coins -> grab
* Leave it -> END

~ hoard_seen
Narrator: The cheap shine slides right off the pile, leaving wet eyeballs, blackened tongues, knucklebones, and one honest wooden box tucked under the guts.
set sk_hoard_seen
-> hoard_menu

~ hoard_blind
Narrator: Gold is gold to a tired eye, and the rubies wink back at you bright as hearth coals.
-> hoard_menu

~ real
if flag.sk_eyeball_dealt
Narrator: You drag the heavy box of raw nuggets free of the offal, and the dead eye at the doorway makes no sound at all.
else
Narrator: As the box comes free, the eye over the doorway bursts into a silent mental shriek that fills the air with a dizzy, dazzling shimmer.
set skitterdeep_alert = now
disadvantage checks 10m: the hypnotic shimmer
endif
gold +450
set sk_hoard_taken
Narrator: Behind you, the butcher's heap heaves up with a wet, giggling whisper.
combat sk_oswald

~ grab
Narrator: Your fingers close on cold, wet eyeballs as the whole butcher's heap erupts into a giggling centipede with a tiny human hand on every leg.
combat sk_oswald
